```mdl
verdict Virtualizer: Placement, useWindow and Window ship in @dxos/react-ui-virtual with the specified props and events.
  status: done
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-virtual/src/placement.ts#Placement, github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-virtual/src/Window.tsx#useWindow, github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-virtual/src/Window.tsx#Window, github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-virtual/src/Window.tsx#WindowProps]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-virtual/src/placement.test.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-virtual/src/Window.stories.tsx]
  walkthrough:
    - Placement holds the anchor and id-keyed measurements as pure arithmetic. github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-virtual/src/placement.ts#Placement
    - useWindow binds it to a host-owned scroller and emits onChange, onEdge and onMismatch. github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-virtual/src/Window.tsx#useWindow
    - Window is the own-scroller binding, composing useFollow for sticky. github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-virtual/src/Window.tsx#Window
  note: |
    `model` is a `WindowModel` (count, getId, subscribe). `sticky` is honoured by `Window` only; `useWindow` leaves following to `useFollow`.
```

